+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+Implement JSON Patch per RFC 6902.
+
+- Export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`; `patch` is an array of operations.
+- Operations: add, remove, replace, move, copy, test. Returns a new document; the input document and the
+  patch are never mutated or aliased by the result.
+- Throws if the patch is not an array, an operation is malformed (not an object, unknown `op`, missing or
+  non-string `path`/`from`, missing `value` for add/replace/test) or an operation fails (target missing,
+  parent missing, array index out of range, `test` mismatch, move into own child).
+- Atomic: any failure throws, no partial result.
+- Pointers follow RFC 6901 (`-` allowed only as add target on arrays); only own properties are used, and
+  `__proto__` members are handled safely.
+- `test` uses deep JSON equality (object member order is irrelevant).
